            "code": {
              "language": "plaintext",
              "showLineNumbers": false,
              "showMiniMap": false
            },
            "content": "## How to read this dashboard\n\nThese counters are **dead-man's switches**, not success/failure metrics. A panel at zero means *that code path stopped running* — the scheduler died, an import broke, a leg was commented out. It does **not** mean a specific call failed. For \"did the backend fail\", read the logs (`_log_giveup` in `llm_client.py`, the `except` around the mhtml leg in `feed.py`).\n\nAlert on **no data**, not on a threshold.\n\n## Why the windows are 8 days and up\n\n`run_scrape_cycle()` fires once a week (Friday 14:00 local, `TARGET_WEEKDAY = 4` in `feed.py`). A 6-hour or 24-hour window would read red for six days out of seven. `$window` defaults to **14d** so two consecutive cycles are always in view — one missed cycle is visible without being ambiguous.\n\n## Metric names\n\nThe OTLP gateway rewrites names on the way into Prometheus: dots become underscores and monotonic counters gain a `_total` suffix. So `scrape_cycle.runs` in `metrics.py` is queried as `scrape_cycle_runs_total` here. Resource attributes become labels: `service.name` → `job`, `service.instance.id` → `instance`.\n\nIf every panel is empty, check the real name first in **Explore**: `{job=\"blogfeed\"}`. If your stack is configured without suffixes, drop `_total` from all seven queries.\n\n## Known gaps\n\n- **A site that stops being captured disappears from the per-site panel** rather than dropping to zero — Prometheus has no series for a label value that stopped being emitted. Read that panel against the site list in `MHTML_SITES_PATH`, not on its own.\n- **`llm.tokens` carries no cost.** The newsfeed pipeline records `nebius.cost_usd` from `config.NEBIUS_MODEL_PRICING`; blogfeed does not. Porting `record_nebius_tokens`'s pricing block into `record_llm_tokens` would let a cost panel drop straight in.\n- **`model` can be an empty string** — `record_llm_tokens` passes `model or \"\"`. The tokens-by-model table maps that to `(model unset)`."
          },
          "pluginVersion": "10.4.0",
          "title": "Notes",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Notes — how to read this, and known gaps",
      "type": "row"
    }
